    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.2,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings level off abruptly at about 0.67–0.70 from 7 h onward, which is typical of a reader that has stopped responding proportionally. The 18 h aliquot was diluted 10x and read twice (mean 0.330, so about 3.30 undiluted). It was also diluted 20x and read twice (mean 0.157, so about 3.13 undiluted). The two diluted results agree within about 5%, so the reader responds proportionally in that range. Corrected for dilution, the 18 h OD is about 3.2, roughly 5 times the undiluted reading of 0.67. The apparent plateau is therefore the instrument's upper limit, not a real stationary phase."
  },
